  "claims": [
    "Arc Tangent shares the existing Circle contact input, source capture, analytic derivative solver and canonical argument parser. The geometry kernel returns solved contact positions, including contacts on extended analytic line supports.",
    "After constructing the supporting circle, a final point chooses the interval between contacts. When three constraints contain exactly two straight curves, those straight contacts are ordered endpoints; their cyclic input order is preserved while the final pick chooses short or long arc orientation. Circles, circular arcs, straight NURBS and a free-point constraint establish this rule.",
    "All 38 qualified successful native workflows and two cancellations compare complete NURBS controls, weights, knots, domains, lengths, closed status, source geometry and selection, and actual Undo/Redo through command and frontend paths on default and native-smlib backends at absolute 1e-6.",
    "Coverage includes two/three contacts, radius locks and the Radius getter, FromFirstPoint, mixed/free points, parallel and reversed-order guides, circles and circular arcs, three-circle sectors, straight NURBS, rotated/translated sources and spatial construction planes.",
    "Fresh captures establish the independent Tangent radius default of 1: ordinary Arc Center and StartPoint constructions do not update it; a successful Tangent construction does. Registry preferences survive model Undo/Redo.",
    "Circle and Arc share an immutable frontend picker and curve/edge pointer routing. Arc caches its supporting circle for final previews. Geometry replacement, deletion, hiding, locking or changed document tolerance resets stale input without retaining temporary objects.",
    "Local checks cover spatial arc sectors, duplicate seam contacts, invalid choices, unchanged source selection, preview/commit equality, cancellation, interruption and failed-command rollback. Shared viewport tests exercise both Circle and Arc with object and surface-edge contacts.",
    "Arc construction options now precede snap shortcuts, so Center is handled as an Arc option at the first prompt. Numeric Arc completion clears command text. Native preference setup workflows exercise both corrections.",
    "A broader regression exposed a stale Pipe face-count assertion. Both Rhino CreateThickPipe and the real Pipe command return four faces for the same thick quarter-arc pipe: two walls and two planar annular ends. Only the stale test expectation changed; Pipe production code is unchanged."
  ],
